Z||000000||FieroPerformance||11-26-2001||07:49 PM||||Well, it isn't very elaborate, I wanted something that would be easy to remove in case I needed the trunk space to haul golf clubs or something. I plan on mounting my amp and possibly a CD changer under the glass and maybe putting a red neon light on the bottom that is wired into the trunk light so it will give the trunk a "show car" effect. I think it cost me about $50-$60 in materials (mainly because of the $40 I spent on plexi glass). The bottom picture was taken before the paint and the top picture is in the trunk with paint. It still needs to be touched up. It fits pretty well considering I had to eye ball the size and trim to fit.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trunkglass.JPG">  <P>I can post more detailed instructions if anyone would like to try to build something like it.<P>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroPerformance (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
